          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Most water heater brands come from a few parent companies: Rheem, A.O. Smith and Bradford White for tanks, with Rinnai, Navien, Noritz and the big tank makers leading tankless. Within those families, the model tier and warranty tell you more than the name on the label.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Choose the heater type and size first, then the brand your installer knows and can service, then the tier with the warranty you want. That order protects you from the cold showers and long waits for parts that cause most regret, whichever logo ends up in your basement.
          </p>
